      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Im having the exact same issues and it is pretty frustrating. I cant click through my action menu at all without it just randomly not inputting.\n\nEdit: Its tied to FPS. If you turn your fps now to something low (like 20) the action menu is completely unusable but even at higher frame rates occasionally the menu wont input.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-09-19T23:58:07.658Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "When selecting items quickly in the action menu on either VR or Desktop, sometimes the input gets ignored. This is caused by new hold-to-activate actions that will take priority over a short click. A click that is held slightly too long is interpreted as a hold, which is then cancelled because it's released before the full hold time. The duration the Action Menu waits before it counts the input as a hold and not a click is far too short to be useful. By convention this is usually a few hundred milliseconds.",
